{"ts": 0.343814, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mStage 4 cleared\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nYou can now\r\n\r\n  ask if a program is there    \u001b[92mcommand -v\u001b[0m\r\n  count lines, count out numbers \u001b[92mwc       \u001b[0m \u001b[92mseq\u001b[0m\r\n  order lines, take the first  \u001b[92msort     \u001b[0m \u001b[92mhead\u001b[0m\r\n  chain commands               \u001b[92m|\u001b[0m\r\n  send output to a file        \u001b[92m>        \u001b[0m \u001b[92m>>\u001b[0m\r\n  match many names             \u001b[92m*\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 379}
{"ts": 0.343903, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "Next: Stage 5 · Ready for vimtutor\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m to go on, or \u001b[92mquit\u001b[93m to stop here. Your place is saved.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 138}
